<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5112" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμείνων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, irreg. 
			Comp. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγαθός,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
			<i>better:</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of persons, <i>stouter,
				stronger, braver,</i> freq. <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, etc.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγ᾽ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.158
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὸν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. vel inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμείνων παντοίας ἀρετάς, ἠμὲν πόδας
					ἠδὲ μάχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.641
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				445
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				337
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ο&lt;&gt;̔ ἀμείνονες</span>
			<i>the better sort,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				627a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμίχλην νυκτὸς ἀμείνω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.11
				</span></i>
			; esp. from <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> downwds., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμεινόν [ἐστι]</span>
			<i>'tis better,</i> either c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεὶ πείθεσθαι ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.274
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1238
			</span></i>, etc.; or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμεινόν ἐστι</span>
			or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γίγνεταί τινι</span> c.
			part., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ σφι ἄμεινον
				γίγνεται τιμωρέουσι</span> if <i>it is good</i> for them
			to assist, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.169
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.118
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.9
			</span></i>: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ τό γ᾽ ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.116
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βουλοίμην . . εἴ τι ἄ. καὶ ὑμῖν καὶ
					ἐμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					19a
				</span></i>
			; freq. with neg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γὰρ
			ἄ.</span> 'twere <i>better</i> not, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				750
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.187
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρήσεται γάρ, εἴτ᾽ ἄ. εἴτε μή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.198
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> neut. as
				Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. πρήσσειν</span>
			to fare <i>better,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.156
			</span></i> sq., etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνήνεικεν Ἀθηναίοις
				ἐπὶ τὸ ἄ.</span> Decr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.77
			</span></i>, cf. Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				43.86
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἀμείνω φρονέειν</span>
			choose the <i>better part,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.145
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖσι τὰ ἀ. ἑάνδανε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					9.19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμεινόνως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					340
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> new 
				Comp.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμεινότερος, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
					<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span> formed from
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμείνων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Mimn.
				14.9
			</span></i>, Poet. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				2.61S.
			</span></i>&lt;</div>
